      "why": "Iterative shares one micro-rotation datapath and needs only N+3 cycles/result. For N in 11..30 and typical Artix-7 Fmax, throughput >=1 MSPS is easily met, so its lower area dominates unrolled_k. It computes identical bits to unrolled_k for the same (data_width, n_iter, angle_guard, frac_guard, rounding), but unrolled_k replicates the datapath k times and lengthens the critical path, so it has strictly larger luts_plus_ffs for the same accuracy and cannot be Pareto-optimal here. W>=11 is the minimum that can satisfy max_abs_err<=2^-10 (output LSB 2^-(W-2)); N>=11 is the minimum for the CORDIC angle residual. Upper bounds cover the high-accuracy/high-area region up to the HV reference area of 1500."
    }
